WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.473
Pedro zigzagged around Great-Aunt Luisa's dark front yard, holding his phone up.

2
00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:10.572
He was trying to get a stronger signal.

3
00:00:10.573 --> 00:00:16.994
Great-Aunt Luisa lived in the countryside, where there wasn't much to do.

4
00:00:16.995 --> 00:00:22.769
Pedro was staying with her for a whole month.

5
00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:27.364
"Are you taking pictures of the moon?" a voice called.

6
00:00:27.365 --> 00:00:31.199
Pedro spotted a girl in a neighbor's yard.

7
00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.940
"No. I was just trying to get a signal."

8
00:00:33.941 --> 00:00:36.190
He glanced upward.

9
00:00:36.191 --> 00:00:41.682
The nearly full moon looked much brighter than it looked at home in the city.

10
00:00:41.683 --> 00:00:48.763
The girl smiled. "I'm Luna. Want to take a look through my telescope?" "Sure."

11
00:00:48.764 --> 00:00:55.213
Pedro walked over to where Luna had set up her telescope. "I've

12
00:00:55.214 --> 00:00:58.841
never seen the moon through a telescope before." "One

13
00:00:58.842 --> 00:01:05.588
day I'd like to see it up close." Luna's eyes shone. "My

14
00:01:05.589 --> 00:01:11.062
dream is to become an astronaut and explore the moon." "You

15
00:01:11.063 --> 00:01:13.557
sure like the moon a lot. Is

16
00:01:13.558 --> 00:01:19.070
it because your name means 'moon' in Spanish?" Pedro asked teasingly. Luna

17
00:01:19.071 --> 00:01:22.485
grinned. "It could be. Hey!

18
00:01:22.486 --> 00:01:25.893
There's a full moon tomorrow. Want

19
00:01:25.894 --> 00:01:28.729
to watch it with me?" Pedro

20
00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:33.373
smiled. "Definitely!" ***

21
00:01:33.374 --> 00:01:38.870
The next night Pedro met Luna in her yard.

22
00:01:38.871 --> 00:01:42.730
"The moon is a different shape tonight," he said.

23
00:01:42.731 --> 00:01:48.564
Luna giggled. "The moon doesn't really change shape, you know.

24
00:01:48.565 --> 00:01:51.856
The sun lights up the moon's surface.

25
00:01:51.857 --> 00:01:58.712
As the moon orbits around Earth, the amount of the sunlit surface we can see changes.

26
00:01:58.713 --> 00:02:02.253
These changes are the phases of the moon."

27
00:02:02.254 --> 00:02:04.999
"Aha," Pedro said.

28
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:09.065
"How long does it take for the moon to orbit Earth?"

29
00:02:09.066 --> 00:02:14.163
"About four weeks—one lunar month," Luna said.

30
00:02:14.164 --> 00:02:18.479
"Oh. Is tonight the start of a lunar month?"

31
00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:24.713
"Nope! The full moon is halfway through a lunar month," Luna explained.

32
00:02:24.714 --> 00:02:28.418
"The new moon is the start of a lunar month. But

33
00:02:28.419 --> 00:02:31.381
it's a confusing name." "Why?"

34
00:02:31.382 --> 00:02:33.964
Pedro asked. "Because

35
00:02:33.965 --> 00:02:38.525
that's when the unlit surface of the moon is facing Earth. We

36
00:02:38.526 --> 00:02:41.700
can't see the moon then." "That

37
00:02:41.701 --> 00:02:46.489
should be called a 'no moon' then!" Pedro grinned. Luna

38
00:02:46.490 --> 00:02:55.470
laughed. "After a new moon, the moon waxes—or looks like it gets bigger. A

39
00:02:55.471 --> 00:02:59.346
few days later, it's a waxing crescent. One

40
00:02:59.347 --> 00:03:04.122
week after the new moon is the first-quarter moon. That's

41
00:03:04.123 --> 00:03:09.921
when half of the moon's surface is visible from Earth." "Why

42
00:03:09.922 --> 00:03:14.189
is it a quarter moon if half of it is visible?" "Because

43
00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:19.534
it's one quarter of the way through the lunar month," Luna said. "Finally

44
00:03:19.535 --> 00:03:24.882
after another week, we have a full moon, like this one. Are

45
00:03:24.883 --> 00:03:27.078
you enjoying it?" Pedro

46
00:03:27.079 --> 00:03:30.560
put his eye to the telescope again. "It's

47
00:03:30.561 --> 00:03:39.316
awesome!" ***

48
00:03:39.317 --> 00:03:46.658
For the next few nights, Pedro and Luna watched the moon slowly seem to disappear.

49
00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:54.255
"It's waning. This is a waning gibbous," Luna explained, pointing to the football-shaped moon.

50
00:03:54.256 --> 00:03:58.398
"In a few days, we'll see the third-quarter moon."

51
00:03:58.399 --> 00:04:04.084
*** Over a week later it was a new moon, and the sky was

52
00:04:04.085 --> 00:04:10.322
moonless. Soon the moon reappeared, and the waxing moon slowly grew

53
00:04:10.323 --> 00:04:18.847
again. One night, under a full moon, Pedro's mom arrived to pick him up.

54
00:04:18.848 --> 00:04:24.407
"Hey, Pedro!" Luna called as Pedro put his stuff into Mom's car.

55
00:04:24.408 --> 00:04:28.486
Luna was holding a big, long box.

56
00:04:28.487 --> 00:04:31.144
"I thought you might like this."

57
00:04:31.145 --> 00:04:35.276
"Whoa! I can't take that," Pedro said.

58
00:04:35.277 --> 00:04:37.593
It was her telescope!

59
00:04:37.594 --> 00:04:39.862
Luna grinned.

60
00:04:39.863 --> 00:04:42.343
"I'm getting a new one soon.

61
00:04:42.344 --> 00:04:46.530
So please take this one."

62
00:04:46.531 --> 00:04:49.395
"Thanks!" Pedro said.

63
00:04:49.396 --> 00:04:52.068
"That's really generous, Luna.

64
00:04:52.069 --> 00:04:55.649
I'm sorry that I don't have anything for you though."

65
00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:59.296
"That's okay." Luna smiled.

66
00:04:59.297 --> 00:05:04.288
"Just promise me we can moon-gaze together when I visit the city."

67
00:05:04.289 --> 00:05:13.421
Pedro smiled back. "Deal!"

